.TE
.PP
Python, TypeScript, and Java use exception classes that extend a
language\-appropriate base (\f[CR]Exception\f[R], \f[CR]Error\f[R],
\f[CR]RuntimeException\f[R] respectively).
C uses negative integer return codes and a thread\-local error message
string.
.SH When each error occurs
\f[B]AuthError\f[R] / \f[CR]BC_ERR_AUTH\f[R]
.PP
Raised when authentication with the server fails.
Causes include:
.IP \(bu 2
The token provided does not match the server\(cqs token.
.IP \(bu 2
The token file is missing or unreadable.
.IP \(bu 2
The server rejected the \f[CR]AUTH\f[R] (v1) or \f[CR]auth\f[R] (v2)
message.
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]SO_PEERCRED\f[R] UID check failed (Unix socket transport).
.PP
\f[B]ProtocolError\f[R] / \f[CR]BC_ERR_PROTOCOL\f[R]
.PP
Raised when the wire protocol is violated.
Causes include:
.IP \(bu 2
An invalid or unrecognized message type was received.
.IP \(bu 2
A v2 frame header has an invalid channel number (outside 0\-5).
.IP \(bu 2
A v2 frame exceeds the 1 MB payload limit.
.IP \(bu 2
JSON parsing failed on a received message.
.IP \(bu 2
The server sent a response for a channel the client did not request.
.IP \(bu 2
NDJSON framing received a line that is not valid JSON.
.PP
\f[B]TimeoutError\f[R] / \f[CR]BC_ERR_TIMEOUT\f[R]
.PP
Raised when an operation exceeds its time limit.
Causes include:
.IP \(bu 2
The connection attempt timed out (TCP or Unix socket connect).
.IP \(bu 2
The authentication handshake did not complete within the timeout.
.IP \(bu 2
An \f[CR]eval\f[R] command did not produce a \f[CR]complete\f[R]
response in time.
.IP \(bu 2
A state or debug request received no response within the timeout.
.PP
\f[B]TransportError\f[R] / \f[CR]BC_ERR_TRANSPORT\f[R]
.PP
Raised when the underlying transport fails.
Causes include:
.IP \(bu 2
The Unix domain socket path does not exist.
.IP \(bu 2
The named pipe could not be opened (Windows Named Pipe transport).
.IP \(bu 2
A \f[CR]read()\f[R] or \f[CR]write()\f[R] returned an unexpected error
(e.g., \f[CR]EPIPE\f[R], \f[CR]ECONNRESET\f[R]).
.IP \(bu 2
The connection was closed unexpectedly by the server.
.IP \(bu 2
File descriptor transport (\f[CR]\-\-fd\f[R]) received an invalid fd
number.
.PP
\f[B]ServerError\f[R] / \f[CR]BC_ERR_SERVER\f[R]
.PP
Raised when the server returns an explicit error response.
Causes include:
.IP \(bu 2
The server sent an \f[CR]error\f[R] message on any v2 channel.
.IP \(bu 2
A v1 \f[CR]ERROR\f[R] response was received.
.IP \(bu 2
The server reported an internal failure (e.g., fork failed).
.PP
In Python, TypeScript, and Java, the \f[CR]ServerError\f[R] exception
carries a \f[B]channel\f[R] attribute indicating which v2 channel
originated the error (see below).
.PP
\f[B]BC_ERR_NOMEM\f[R] (C only)
.PP
Returned when a memory allocation (\f[CR]malloc\f[R],
\f[CR]realloc\f[R], \f[CR]strdup\f[R]) fails.
This is C\-specific because Python, TypeScript, and Java handle memory
allocation failures through their own runtime mechanisms
(\f[CR]MemoryError\f[R], heap exhaustion, \f[CR]OutOfMemoryError\f[R]).
.PP
\f[B]BC_ERR_PARAM\f[R] (C only)
.PP
Returned when a function receives an invalid parameter.
Examples:
.IP \(bu 2
A \f[CR]NULL\f[R] pointer where a non\-null argument is required.
.IP \(bu 2
A negative timeout value.
.IP \(bu 2
A channel number outside the valid range.
.PP
This is C\-specific because the other languages use their own parameter
validation (Python \f[CR]TypeError\f[R]/\f[CR]ValueError\f[R],
TypeScript compile\-time checks, Java
\f[CR]IllegalArgumentException\f[R]).
.SH ServerError channel attribute
In Python, TypeScript, and Java, \f[CR]ServerError\f[R] (and its
language equivalents) includes a \f[B]channel\f[R] property identifying
which v2 channel the error originated from:
.PP
